        drivingExperience: "The 136hp CJCB offers a remarkably refined, smooth, and quiet driving experience. It is heavily geared toward fuel economy. The 320 Nm of torque provides decent punch in city traffic, but it runs out of breath quickly on the highway or when overtaking. The engine practically begs to be mapped to unleash its true potential, as it is artificially choked by the factory software.",
        mechanicVerdict: "The CJCB 2.0 TDI EA189 is an incredibly robust engine block. While Audi improved the oil pump hex shaft on these later models, it can still round off at high mileages. The CP4 high-pressure fuel pump remains a known failure point that can total the fuel system. If you proactively protect the CP4 pump with a bypass kit and maintain it well, this engine will easily reach 350,000+ km. Flash it to Stage 1 to remove the software restrictions, and you have a phenomenal, highly reliable daily driver.",
        repairCostEstimate: "$500 - $1000 / year (Assuming preventative mods are done)",
