        oilSpecification: "VW 507.00 (5W-30 Fully Synthetic)",
        commonIssues: [ "CP4.1 HPFP Failure: The absolute defining nightmare of the EA189 engine. The Bosch CP4 fuel pump wears internally, sending microscopic metal shavings through the entire fuel system. Requires a complete fuel system replacement if it fails.", "Oil Pump Hex Shaft Rounding: The balance shaft module uses a metal hex key to drive the oil pump. It rounds off over time, instantly killing oil pressure and destroying the turbo and engine.", "DPF Clogging: The factory DPF creates immense backpressure. If driven primarily in the city, it clogs rapidly, forcing the car into limp mode.", "EGR Cooler Failure: The Exhaust Gas Recirculation cooler clogs with soot and can crack internally, leaking coolant into the exhaust system.", "Dual Mass Flywheel (DMF) Wear: The DMF springs weaken over time, causing a noticeable vibration and clunking noise at idle or when shutting off the engine.", "Intake Manifold Flap Actuator: The plastic mechanism controlling the swirl flaps wears out, throwing a P2015 check engine light." ],
